From: beitlab Robotics MilkV duo OS <image/patches>
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] buildroot: duos arm64 sd playground rootfs

Local change to configs/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd_defconfig.

- Init: systemd (PROMPT.md requires rtos-agent.service). Buildroot 2025.02
  systemd depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_GCC_AT_LEAST_8; the SDK's external
  Linaro 7.3.1 toolchain cannot provide it, so the rootfs toolchain is the
  Buildroot-listed Bootlin "aarch64 glibc stable 2024.05-1" (gcc 13, kernel
  headers 4.19 <= the 5.10 kernel). The kernel, u-boot, FSBL and SDK
  middleware are still built with host-tools as before; their glibc
  binaries keep working on the newer glibc.
- Identity: hostname beitlab-milkv-duo, root password playground.
- SSH: OpenSSH replaces Dropbear (and gesftpserver, whose sftp-server
  OpenSSH provides). sshd_config comes from the playground overlay.
- mDNS: avahi-daemon.
- No Python on the device (PROMPT.md "Agent").
- dnsmasq removed: under systemd it would start a DHCP server on the
  Ethernet LAN; the stock image only ran it for USB RNDIS, which this
  image does not configure.
- systemd-networkd/resolved off: dhcpcd (already in the stock image) keeps
  configuring eth0.
---
diff --git a/buildroot/configs/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd_defconfig b/buildroot/configs/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd_defconfig
index 52613a97..0bdd04fd 100644
--- a/buildroot/configs/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd_defconfig
+++ b/buildroot/configs/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd_defconfig
@@ -1,19 +1,13 @@
 BR2_aarch64=y
 BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL=y
-BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_CUSTOM=y
-BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_PATH="$(TOPDIR)/../host-tools/gcc/gcc-linaro-7.3.1-2018.05-x86_64_aarch64-linux-gnu"
-BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_CUSTOM_PREFIX="aarch64-linux-gnu"
-BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_GCC_7=y
-BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_HEADERS_4_10=y
-BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_CUSTOM_GLIBC=y
-BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_CXX=y
-BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_FORTRAN=y
-BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_OPENMP=y
+BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN=y
+BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN_AARCH64_GLIBC_STABLE=y
 BR2_OPTIMIZE_S=y
